// Names resolve in the right scope around an option that comes from an insertion:
// a beat parameter of the inserted beat shadows a temporary state of the parent
// with the same name, each beat keeps its own persistent state, and a local beat
// of the inserted beat can be called from the option body.

beat Start
  new state
    mood: "start-temp"
  state
    visits: 0
  visits = visits + 1
  choice
    Stay
      Stayed with mood $mood.
    + Side("param")
  Start epilogue: mood $mood, visits $visits.

beat Side(mood)
  state
    visits: 10
  visits = visits + 1

  beat Local
    Local beat sees $mood and visits $visits.

  choice
    Use local
      Local()

      Side option: mood $mood, visits $visits.
  Side epilogue: mood $mood, visits $visits.

/*
<test>
- choices: [0]
  expected: |
    + Stay
    + Use local

    ~ Stayed with mood start-temp.

    ~ Start epilogue: mood start-temp, visits 1.
- choices: [1]
  expected: |
    + Stay
    + Use local

    ~ Local beat sees param and visits 11.

    ~ Side option: mood param, visits 11.

    ~ Side epilogue: mood param, visits 11.

    ~ Start epilogue: mood start-temp, visits 1.
- choices: [1]
  saveAtChoice: 0
  saveAtDialogue: 0
  expected: |
    + Stay
    + Use local

    + Stay
    + Use local

    ~ Local beat sees param and visits 11.

    ~ Local beat sees param and visits 11.

    ~ Side option: mood param, visits 11.

    ~ Side epilogue: mood param, visits 11.

    ~ Start epilogue: mood start-temp, visits 1.
- choices: [1]
  saveAtDialogue: [2, 3]
  expected: |
    + Stay
    + Use local

    ~ Local beat sees param and visits 11.

    ~ Side option: mood param, visits 11.

    ~ Side epilogue: mood param, visits 11.

    ~ Side epilogue: mood param, visits 11.

    ~ Start epilogue: mood start-temp, visits 1.

    ~ Start epilogue: mood start-temp, visits 1.
</test>
*/
